{"cti_reasoning":"The state sp=7, hwm=9 satisfies P because the guard sp==4'd8 is false, but it violates R (hwm<=4'd8 and hwm>=sp are fine, hwm<=8 is broken). With ce low the design sits in this state for any number of cycles; then one enabled push takes sp to 8 while the high-water update (nxt=8 > hwm=9 is false) leaves hwm at 9, so in the next state sp==4'd8 with hwm!=4'd8 and P fails.","cti_state":[{"signal":"sp","value":"4'd7"},{"signal":"hwm","value":"4'd9"}],"invariants":["sp <= 4'd8","hwm <= 4'd8","hwm >= sp"],"verilog":"module stack_hwm (
