{"cti_reasoning":"The state found=1, idx=2'd1 satisfies P because idx is nonzero, but violates R since the found flag is only allowed to be set when idx has reached 2'd3. The search engine is not frozen there (idx != 3), so with ce=1 and a non-matching character idx resets to 2'd0 while found stays sticky at 1, giving found && idx==0 and breaking P; with ce=0 the design sits in this state for any number of cycles.","cti_state":[{"signal":"idx","value":"2'd1"},{"signal":"found","value":"1'b1"},{"signal":"rst","value":"1'b0"}],"invariants":["!found || idx == 2'd3","idx != 2'd3 || found"],"verilog":"module substr_search (
