{"cti_reasoning":"State S has the one-hot priority pointer parked on bit 3 while the binary index register says 1, so the low-half flag (pri[0]|pri[1]) is 0 and idx[1] is 0 — the property holds (and holds vacuously while req is 0 and step is low, so the design can idle here forever). S violates the invariant because pri is not 4'b0001<<idx. One rotate step yields pri=4'b0001 with idx=2'd2, and then any request on line 0 makes gnt nonzero with low-half flag 1 and idx[1] 1, breaking the property.","cti_state":[{"signal":"pri","value":"4'b1000"},{"signal":"idx","value":"2'd1"},{"signal":"req","value":"4'b0000"},{"signal":"step","value":"1'b0"}],"invariants":["pri == (4'b0001 << idx)"],"verilog":"module rr_arbiter_pri (
