{"cti_reasoning": "In state S the north-south light is RED and the east-west light is GREEN, so the guarded property (NS green implies EW not green) holds vacuously; but S violates R because at phase 5 (the all-red interval before the NS green handover) the EW light must already be RED. With ce low the controller sits in S indefinitely; one enabled step with timer==0 advances phase 5 -> 0 and increments the NS light RED->GREEN while EW stays GREEN, making both roads green and breaking P.", "cti_state": [{"signal": "phase", "value": "3'd5"}, {"signal": "timer", "value": "3'd0"}, {"signal": "ns_state", "value": "2'd0"}, {"signal": "ew_state", "value": "2'd1"}], "invariants": ["phase <= 3'd5", "timer <= 3'd4", "ns_state == ((phase == 3'd0) ? 2'd1 : (phase == 3'd1) ? 2'd2 : 2'd0)", "ew_state == ((phase == 3'd3) ? 2'd1 : (phase == 3'd4) ? 2'd2 : 2'd0)"], "verilog": "// Two-road intersection controller.
