{"cti_reasoning": "State S has prog=3'd3 while the shadow one-hot register sits in state 0 (hot=5'b00001) and the 4-bit capture window is all zeros, so S satisfies both assertions (detect=0 equals hot[4]=0, and prog!=4 so the window clause is vacuous) yet violates R (hot != 1<<prog, and prog==3 without win[2:0]==3'b110). With i_ce low the design holds prog, hot, win and detect unchanged forever, so the solver can stall in S for the whole induction window; then one cycle with i_ce=1, i_bit=1 drives prog to 3'd4 (so detect latches 1 and the window clause becomes active with win=4'b0001) while hot only advances 5'b00001 -> 5'b00010 (hot[4]=0), breaking both assertions at once.", "cti_state": [{"signal": "prog", "value": "3'd3"}, {"signal": "hot", "value": "5'b00001"}, {"signal": "win", "value": "4'b0000"}, {"signal": "detect", "value": "1'b0"}, {"signal": "i_ce", "value": "1'b1 (on the violating step; 1'b0 while stalling)"}, {"signal": "i_bit", "value": "1'b1 (on the violating step)"}], "invariants": ["prog <= 3'd4", "hot == (5'b00001 << prog)", "prog != 3'd1 || win[0] == 1'b1", "prog != 3'd2 || win[1:0] == 2'b11", "prog != 3'd3 || win[2:0] == 3'b110", "prog != 3'd4 || win == 4'b1101"], "verilog": "// Serial debug-link pattern probe: detects the fixed 4-bit sync pattern 1101
