{"cti_reasoning": "In the CTI state the window register win is high and the one-hot phase register dec is 5'b00001, so dec is non-zero and P (win implies |dec) holds; but state is the illegal encoding 3'd5, violating both R clauses (state<=4, and dec == 5'b00001<<state which at state 5 would be 0). The design can sit in this state indefinitely with i_ce low, and one step with i_ce high takes the default branch of the case, which keeps state illegal and loads dec with 5'b00000 while win stays set (win only clears from S_WRITE), so P fails in the next cycle.", "cti_state": [{"signal": "state", "value": "3'd5"}, {"signal": "dec", "value": "5'b00001"}, {"signal": "win", "value": "1'b1"}], "invariants": ["state <= 3'd4", "dec == (5'b00001 << state)"], "verilog": "module fsm_phase_window (
