{"cti_reasoning": "In the named state the output register is delivering ARM, so neither the FINISH nor the START assertion is triggered and P holds, and the design can sit there indefinitely with step=0; but the skid buffer illegally holds FINISH instead of the chain successor START of the word currently in the output register, which violates the skid-ordering clause of R. With step=1 and out_ready=1 the ARM word retires (phase becomes 1) and the skid word is pushed into the output register, giving out_valid=1, out_code=FINISH while phase==1, which violates the FINISH assertion the very next cycle. A mirror-image state (out_code=FINISH, phase=2, skid_code=START) breaks the START assertion the same way, so neither assertion is inductive alone.", "cti_state": [{"signal": "out_valid", "value": "1'b1"}, {"signal": "out_code", "value": "2'd1"}, {"signal": "skid_valid", "value": "1'b1"}, {"signal": "skid_code", "value": "2'd3"}, {"signal": "phase", "value": "2'd0"}, {"signal": "src_phase", "value": "2'd2"}], "invariants": ["phase <= 2'd2", "src_phase <= 2'd2", "!skid_valid || out_valid", "!out_valid || out_code == phase + 2'd1", "!skid_valid || skid_code == ((phase == 2'd2) ? 2'd1 : ((phase == 2'd1) ? 2'd3 : 2'd2))", "out_valid || src_phase == phase", "!out_valid || skid_valid || src_phase == ((phase == 2'd2) ? 2'd0 : phase + 2'd1)", "!skid_valid || src_phase == ((phase == 2'd0) ? 2'd2 : phase - 2'd1)"], "verilog": "// Valid/ready pipeline stage with a skid buffer carrying a three-step
// command chain: ARM -> START -> FINISH -> ARM -> ...
