{"cti_reasoning": "The state count=5, wptr=3, rptr=0 satisfies P (count <= 5) but violates R because the occupancy register disagrees with the pointer difference (5 != 3). Since full is derived from the pointers only, full is false there, so with i_ce low the design idles in this state forever and a single push (i_ce=1, push=1) increments count to 6, breaking P.", "cti_state": [{"signal": "count", "value": "4'd5"}, {"signal": "wptr", "value": "3'd3"}, {"signal": "rptr", "value": "3'd0"}], "invariants": ["count == {1'b0, (wptr - rptr)}", "(wptr - rptr) <= 3'd5"], "verilog": "module alu_result_fifo (
