{"cti_reasoning": "The state S has state = 4'd7, an unreachable binary encoding of the flow FSM, while the activity mirror still holds 8'h01, so the property (mirror bit 7 clear and mirror nonzero) is satisfied, but the relation mirror == (8'b1 << state) and the bound state <= 4'd6 are both false. With ce low the design sits in S forever, and one enabled step drives mirror <= (8'b1 << nxt) with nxt == state == 4'd7, giving mirror = 8'h80 while tracking is still set, so the property fails in the next state.", "cti_state": [{"signal": "state", "value": "4'd7"}, {"signal": "mirror", "value": "8'h01"}, {"signal": "tracking", "value": "1'b1"}], "invariants": ["state <= 4'd6", "mirror == (8'b1 << state)"], "verilog": "module pcb_flow_fsm (
    input  wire       clk,
    input  wire       rst,
    input  wire       ce,        // pipeline step enable; low => everything idles
    input  wire       start,     // requirements accepted
    input  wire       route_ok,  // router reported a completed board
