{"cti_reasoning": "State wd=8 with expired=1 satisfies P (expired implies wd[3] is set, and 8 has bit 3 set) but violates R, which ties the flag exactly to the saturated counter value (expired == (wd == 12)); the design can idle there indefinitely with i_ce low, and one cycle with i_ce and i_feed high takes the partial-credit path (gated on wd != LIMIT, not on the flag), dropping wd to 4 while expired stays 1, so wd[3] becomes 0 and P fails.", "cti_state": [{"signal": "wd", "value": "4'd8"}, {"signal": "expired", "value": "1'b1"}, {"signal": "pos", "value": "8'd5"}], "invariants": ["wd <= 4'd12", "expired == (wd == 4'd12)"], "verilog": "module wdog_scan (
