{"cti_reasoning": "The state has pend=4'b0001 but the shadow occupancy counter pcnt=4 and the locked owner is index 1 whose pending bit is clear, so it violates R (pcnt != popcount(pend), and lock without pend[owner]); it still satisfies P because with ce held low nothing moves, so pend and pcnt are both stable and pcnt<=4. One step with ce=1, rel=1, req=0 clears the already-clear bit of owner 1 (pend stays 4'b0001, i.e. still $stable) while pcnt is decremented to 3, so the guard $stable(pend) holds but $stable(pcnt) fails and P breaks.", "cti_state": [{"signal": "pend", "value": "4'b0001"}, {"signal": "pcnt", "value": "3'd4"}, {"signal": "lock", "value": "1'b1"}, {"signal": "owner", "value": "2'd1"}, {"signal": "pv", "value": "1'b1"}, {"signal": "$past(pend)", "value": "4'b0001"}, {"signal": "$past(pcnt)", "value": "3'd4"}], "invariants": ["pcnt == ({2'd0,pend[0]} + {2'd0,pend[1]} + {2'd0,pend[2]} + {2'd0,pend[3]})", "!lock || pend[owner]", "pcnt <= 3'd4"], "verilog": "module arb_lock_pending (
