{"cti_reasoning": "The state S has busy_cr=1 (a credit sitting at the consumer) while the chain-history flags ever_arm/ever_start are still 0 and ever_fin=0, so the property (nf && ever_fin -> ever_arm && ever_start) holds vacuously; S violates R because the credit sum is 3+0+1=4 instead of the configured total 3 (and it also violates 'ever_start || busy_cr==0'). With i_ce=0 the design idles in S forever, and one step with i_ce=1, i_done=1 takes the finish transition (legal since busy_cr!=0), setting ever_fin=1 while ever_arm and ever_start are still 0, so P fails in the successor state.", "cti_state": [{"signal": "free_cr", "value": "4'd3"}, {"signal": "armed_cr", "value": "4'd0"}, {"signal": "busy_cr", "value": "4'd1"}, {"signal": "ever_arm", "value": "1'b0"}, {"signal": "ever_start", "value": "1'b0"}, {"signal": "ever_fin", "value": "1'b0"}, {"signal": "nf", "value": "1'b1"}], "invariants": ["free_cr <= 4'd3", "armed_cr <= 4'd3", "busy_cr <= 4'd3", "free_cr + armed_cr + busy_cr == 4'd3", "ever_arm || free_cr == 4'd3", "ever_start || busy_cr == 4'd0"], "verilog": "// Credit-managed transfer engine: three credit pools, one per chain step.
// A credit is spent on ARM, handed on at START and returned by the consumer
// at FINISH.  Total credits in the system is fixed at TOTAL by construction.
module credit_chain (
