{"cti_reasoning": "S has the stability flag asserted while the consecutive-sample counter is only 2, which is impossible by construction (the flag is the decoded form of cnt==K), yet S satisfies P vacuously because the arming window register is still clear; with i_ce low the design sits in S forever. One step with i_ce=1, i_arm=1 and i_raw==samp latches armed=1 while the $past shadows capture stable_f=1 with cnt=3'd2, so the assertion !$past(stable_f) || $past(cnt) >= 3 fails.", "cti_state": [{"signal": "cnt", "value": "3'd2"}, {"signal": "stable_f", "value": "1'b1"}, {"signal": "samp", "value": "1'b0"}, {"signal": "o_clean", "value": "1'b0"}, {"signal": "armed", "value": "1'b0"}, {"signal": "pv", "value": "1'b1"}, {"signal": "$past(cnt)", "value": "3'd2"}, {"signal": "$past(stable_f)", "value": "1'b1"}], "invariants": ["cnt <= 3'd5", "stable_f == (cnt == 3'd5)"], "verilog": "module sample_debouncer (
