{"cti_reasoning": "In state S the registered status flag full_q is 0 so the property's rising edge guard is false and P holds, but the redundant outstanding register out_r holds 8 while the issued/retired counters are equal, so the accounting relation (iss-ret)==out_r is violated. The design idles in S with i_ce low for as many cycles as the induction window needs; a single step with i_ce high and no issue/retire re-registers the flags from the same stale state, so full_q rises to 1 (because out_r==8) while empty_q is loaded with (iss==ret)==1, making full and empty assert together and breaking P.", "cti_state": [{"signal": "iss", "value": "5'd5"}, {"signal": "ret", "value": "5'd5"}, {"signal": "out_r", "value": "4'd8"}, {"signal": "full_q", "value": "1'b0"}, {"signal": "empty_q", "value": "1'b1"}, {"signal": "mon", "value": "1'b1"}, {"signal": "pv", "value": "1'b1"}], "invariants": ["(iss - ret) == {1'b0, out_r}", "out_r <= 4'd8"], "verilog": "module sb_window (
