{"cti_reasoning": "The state acc_s=8'h00, acc_c=8'h01, total=8'h00 satisfies P because acc_s[0]==total[0]==0, but it violates R since the carry half has its bit 0 set (and the two halves no longer sum to total); the design can sit in it forever with i_ce low, and one accumulate step with i_data=8'h00 gives acc_s=8'h01 while total stays 8'h00, so acc_s[0] != total[0] and P fails.", "cti_state": [{"signal": "acc_s", "value": "8'h00"}, {"signal": "acc_c", "value": "8'h01"}, {"signal": "total", "value": "8'h00"}, {"signal": "i_ce", "value": "1'b1"}, {"signal": "i_clear", "value": "1'b0"}, {"signal": "i_data", "value": "8'h00"}], "invariants": ["acc_c[0] == 1'b0", "(acc_s + acc_c) == total"], "verilog": "module csa_accum_parity (
