{"cti_reasoning": "The state prog=2 with seen_half=0 satisfies P (P only constrains prog==3) but violates R, which says any progress of 2 or more implies the shadow register seen_half was already latched; with i_ce low the detector sits in this state forever, and one enabled step with sym=1 advances prog to 3 while seen_half stays 0 (it is only set when the *next* progress equals 2), so before_alarm is still 1 and the precedence property fails.", "cti_state": [{"signal": "prog", "value": "3'd2"}, {"signal": "seen_half", "value": "1'b0"}, {"signal": "before_alarm", "value": "1'b1"}, {"signal": "alarm", "value": "1'b0"}], "invariants": ["prog <= 3'd3", "prog < 3'd2 || seen_half"], "verilog": "module chess_clock_seq_alarm (
    input  wire clk,
