{"cti_reasoning": "State S has busy=1 with ttl=5'd1 and acc_cnt=4'd0: it satisfies P because ttl != 0 while busy, but it violates R, which requires ttl == 13 - acc_cnt (i.e. 13) whenever busy is set. With i_ce low the lane sits in S forever, and one enabled accumulate step decrements ttl to 0 while acc_cnt only reaches 1 (so busy stays set, since the lane only finishes at acc_cnt==12), which makes P false in the very next state.", "cti_state": [{"signal": "busy", "value": "1'b1"}, {"signal": "ttl", "value": "5'd1"}, {"signal": "acc_cnt", "value": "4'd0"}, {"signal": "o_done", "value": "1'b0"}], "invariants": ["acc_cnt <= 4'd12", "ttl <= 5'd13", "!busy || (ttl == 5'd13 - {1'b0, acc_cnt})", "!busy || acc_cnt <= 4'd11"], "verilog": "module npu_psum_lane (
