{"cti_reasoning": "The state phase=P_IDLE(2'd0), busy=0, cnt=3'd0 satisfies both assertions (busy is low so the timeout wire is low, and the guard phase==2'd1 is false), but it violates the relation because the deadline register holds 0 instead of a value in [1,4]; with i_ce low the design sits there forever, and one step with i_ce=1, start=1 moves it to phase=P_REQ with busy=1 and cnt still 3'd0, which makes timeout=1 (P1 fails) and puts an out-of-range deadline in the request phase (P2 fails).", "cti_state": [{"signal": "phase", "value": "2'd0"}, {"signal": "busy", "value": "1'b0"}, {"signal": "cnt", "value": "3'd0"}], "invariants": ["cnt >= 3'd1", "cnt <= 3'd4", "busy == (phase != 2'd0)"], "verilog": "module handshake_deadline (
