{"cti_reasoning": "In S the window is open (armed=1) and cnt=4'd1, so both assertions hold vacuously (cnt is neither 0 nor 8), yet cnt=1 while pend=8'b10000010 has two set bits, violating R. With i_ce low nothing changes, so the solver can sit in S for the whole induction window; one tick with i_ce=1, i_req=0 retires the bit leaving bit 7, giving cnt=0 while pend=8'b00000100 is still non-empty, which breaks the first assertion (the symmetric state cnt=4'd7, pend=8'b00111111 with i_req=1 breaks the second).", "cti_state": [{"signal": "armed", "value": "1'b1"}, {"signal": "pend", "value": "8'b10000010"}, {"signal": "cnt", "value": "4'd1"}, {"signal": "i_ce", "value": "1'b0"}], "invariants": ["cnt == (pend[0]+pend[1]+pend[2]+pend[3]+pend[4]+pend[5]+pend[6]+pend[7])", "cnt <= 4'd8"], "verilog": "module clock_pend_track (
