{"cti_reasoning": "In state S the LFSR register holds all-zeros with the chain FSM armed and the before-scope register pre_done still high; P holds in S because while ce is low nothing moves at all, so lfsr and stage are both stable each cycle. S violates R (lfsr != 0) and is therefore unreachable in real operation, but from S a single step with ce=1 and start=1 feeds the all-zeros lockup value back into the LFSR (lfsr stays 4'd0, so $stable(lfsr) is true) while stage advances ARMED->RUNNING, so $stable(stage) is false and P fails in the very next state.", "cti_state": [{"signal": "lfsr", "value": "4'd0"}, {"signal": "stage", "value": "2'd1"}, {"signal": "pre_done", "value": "1'b1"}, {"signal": "pv", "value": "1'b1"}, {"signal": "chal", "value": "4'd0"}], "invariants": ["lfsr != 4'd0"], "verilog": "// Debug-probe challenge sequencer: a maximal-length LFSR supplies one tick per
