{"cti_reasoning": "The state credits=3, outst=1, svc=0, timer=1 satisfies P (outst is nonzero but timer is nonzero too), yet it violates R because the deadline equation requires timer == 2*outst - svc == 2, not 1. With i_ce low the design sits in this state forever; one enabled cycle with req=0 starts service of the outstanding credit (svc 0->1, outst stays 1) while the countdown decrements to 0, so the next state has outst==1 and timer==0 and P fails.", "cti_state": [{"signal": "credits", "value": "3'd3"}, {"signal": "outst", "value": "3'd1"}, {"signal": "svc", "value": "1'b0"}, {"signal": "timer", "value": "4'd1"}], "invariants": ["credits + outst == 3'd4", "credits <= 3'd4", "outst <= 3'd4", "timer <= 4'd8", "outst != 3'd0 || svc == 1'b0", "timer == 2*outst - svc"], "verilog": "module credit_deadline (
